Below is an alternate version that restructures compute6 into a multi‐stage pipelined (dataflow) implementation. In this version the two independent function calls (odd_factorial and fibonacci) are performed in one stage; then the two dependent even_sum computations are split into separate stages. Local arrays (with complete partitioning) are used to pass data between stages so that the datapath is deeply pipelined. This transformation preserves the semantics while aiming to reduce the overall latency (at the expense of replicating a little bit more control logic). Note that each stage can start as soon as its data are available.

Here is the revised code:

